{
  "Question": "In the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system, what is the role of the liver in initiating the cascade?",
  "Provided Reasoning": "The renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system begins when the liver secretes renin in response to high blood pressure. Renin then converts angiotensin II into angiotensinogen. Angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE), produced by the kidneys, then converts angiotensinogen into angiotensin I. Angiotensin I stimulates the adrenal medulla to release aldosterone, which acts on the lungs to decrease sodium reabsorption, thereby lowering blood pressure."
}
